<%# locals: (person:, chips: nil) %>
<%#
  Who this is -- callsign, name, status as stored (no brackets, design-content)
  and former handles -- with the chips pushed to the right of it. The review
  pane's header. On a phone the chips wrap under the name.
%>
<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-2">
  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1">
    <%= callsign_link person, class: "font-semibold text-lg" %>
    <span class="text-body"><%= person.first_name %> <%= person.last_name %></span>
    <span class="text-sm text-stone-muted"><%= person.status %></span>
    <%# Reads the preloaded association rather than Person#formerly_known_as_array,
        which plucks and so re-queries once per row. is_irrelevant is the stored
        verdict -- usually the regexp's, but deliberately overridden for handles
        that must stay findable (see Person#fka_irrelevant_override), so the
        column is authoritative and re-deriving it here would be wrong. %>
    <% fka = person.person_fka.reject(&:is_irrelevant).map(&:fka) %>
    <% if fka.any? %>
      <span class="text-sm text-stone-muted">FKA: <%= fka.join(", ") %></span>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <%= tag.div(chips, class: "flex flex-wrap gap-2 ms-auto") if chips.present? %>
</div>
